  "findings": [
    "Known rarity values 1/2/3/4 compare row quantity against 4/3/2/1. Values 0/5 set false; other byte values reach return without writing isOK. Test seeds expose this unwritten output, not an asserted client default.",
    "Min/max helpers enumerate 13 indices via runtime enum services, look up user-friendly labels in JSON, compare supplied Map_Find values, and report the first failing enumerated type. Actual enum display names and missing-map/JSON error behavior remain services, not proven facts.",
    "Aggregation skips other deck IDs, rejects set 3 or negative regular/gold quantities, then counts each row independently. Zero quantities still visit later metadata/flag checks; rows are not merged inside this block.",
    "Faction list collection bypasses neutral and nonzero-exile cases. Ally count/elite checks use supplied main/static/exile faction values, with neutral and matching-exile exemptions.",
    "Ownership compares combined regular/gold quantities per row against supplied collection entry; reservation is sticky after first true. Location detection here uses the card-name prefix, not the supplied Type value.",
    "These observations are not defects without upstream input normalization and library/native authority. No simulator production code was changed."
  ],
